description: Measurement fields for specimens in a Herpetology catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 3
  badge:
    text: Beta
    variant: caution
---

Specimens in the `Herpetology` catalog format show the herpetofauna measurement
form. Weight units, sex, and life stage work the same way across taxon groups;
see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="caution" %}

Herpetology support is in beta. Check exports against your collection's
requirements before relying on them.

{% /aside %}

## Measurements

- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex controlled vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage controlled vocabulary.
- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `SVL (cm)`: snout-vent length.
- `Remarks`: additional notes about the specimen.

## Parts and symbionts

Herpetofauna catalogs include the `Symbionts` examination fields at the bottom
of the measurement form and the symbiont tab in `Specimen Parts`. See
[Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).
